# Skill junctions — what is linked here, and how to restore what is not

<!-- Copy to .claude/skills/RELINK.md in your project (the folder is usually gitignored). Fill in the date,
     versions and the keep-list. The point: after `setupAgenticToolkit("update")` renames skills, you can
     rebuild the links from a written list instead of guessing. -->

Pruned <YYYY-MM-DD> from <N> entries to <M>. Built against matlab <version> / simulink <version> catalogs.

## Why the prune
This machine has only <MATLAB, Simulink, ...> licensed. Skills for other toolboxes load into every session's
context and can never run.

## Kept
| Source | Count | What |
|---|---|---|
| `simulink/skills-catalog/**` | all | whole Simulink catalog (a skill that says "needs a licence you lack" beats silence) |
| `matlab/skills-catalog/matlab-core` | 7 | ... |
| <more groups> | | |

Not from any catalog: local skills (`simulink-tile-layout`, ...) and loose cheat-sheets
(`simulink-interaction.md`, `-modeling.md`, `-simulation.md`, `-baseline-test.md`; no frontmatter on purpose).

## Restore one skill / a group (Git Bash, Windows)
```bash
cd <project>/.claude/skills
T="$HOME/.matlab/agentic-toolkits"
s="$T/matlab/skills-catalog/<group>/<skill>"
cmd //c mklink //J "$(basename "$s")" "$(cygpath -w "$s")"      # //J, not /J ; cygpath -w, never hand-escaped
```
Restart Claude Code afterwards.

## After a toolkit update
`setupAgenticToolkit("update", Prompt=false)` — **Prompt=false is mandatory from an agent session.**
Delete every junction, recreate from this list, then check for BROKEN links (mklink succeeds even when the
target does not exist). Restart Claude Code (a new MCP server binary only loads at session start).
